# ClearWay environment configuration
#
# CURRENT STATUS: ClearWay needs NO API keys and NO .env file.
#   - Geocoding uses the public OpenStreetMap Nominatim service
#   - Routing uses the community "routed-foot" endpoint
#   - Pedestrian infrastructure uses the OpenStreetMap Overpass API
# All three are keyless; see src/geocoding.py, src/routing.py and
# src/osm_data.py. Nothing in this project ever reads a .env file.
#
# If you later switch to a keyed provider (for example OpenRouteService), add
# python-dotenv to requirements.txt and load the file explicitly:
#
#     from dotenv import load_dotenv
#     load_dotenv()
#     key = os.environ["OPENROUTESERVICE_API_KEY"]
#
# Until that code exists, the lines below are INACTIVE documentation only.
# Do not put real keys in a tracked file, and never put them in frontend code.
# If you do add a .env locally, keep it git-ignored.
#
# ---- INACTIVE: only relevant once a keyed provider is wired up -------------
# OPENROUTESERVICE_API_KEY=
# ROUTING_API_KEY=
#
# ---- INACTIVE: pattern for a keyed geocoder -------------------------------
# GEOCODING_API_KEY=
